        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
        "@value": 352
      }
    ],
    "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/text": [
      {
        "@value": "1030.16.2 Handrail termination. Handrails located on the side of stepped aisles shall return to a wall, guard or the walking surface or shall be continuous to the handrail of an adjacent stepped aisle flight."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://example.org/ibc/2021/sem-ibc2021-1015.7-atomic-1",
    "@type": [
      "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/AtomicRule"
    ],
    "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/modality": [
      {
        "@value": "shall"
      }
    ],
    "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/statementType": [
      {
        "@value": "obligation"
      }
    ],
    "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/text": [
      {
        "@value": "Guards shall be provided where the roof hatch opening is located within 10 feet (3048 mm) of a roof edge or open side of a walking surface and such edge or open side is located more than 30 inches (762 mm) above the floor, roof or grade below."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://example.org/ibc/2021/sem-ibc2021-1011.5.4.1-atomic-1",
    "@type": [
      "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/AtomicRule"
    ],
    "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/modality": [
      {
        "@value": "may"
      }
    ],
    "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/statementType": [
      {
        "@value": "permission"
      }
    ],
    "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/text": [
      {
        "@value": "Where the bottom or top riser adjoins a sloping public way, walkway or driveway having an established grade and serving as a landing, the bottom or top riser is permitted to be reduced along the slope to less than 4 inches (102 mm) in height, with the variation in height of the bottom or top riser not to exceed one unit vertical in 12 units horizontal (8-percent slope) of stair width."
      }
    ]
  },
