        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
        "@value": 311
      }
    ],
    "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/text": [
      {
        "@value": "1007.1.1 Two exits or exit access doorways. Where two exits, exit access doorways, exit access stairways or ramps, or any combination thereof, are required from any portion of the exit access, they shall be placed a distance apart equal to not less than one-half of the length of the maximum overall diagonal dimension of the building or area to be served measured in a straight line between them. Interlocking or scissor stairways shall be counted as one exit stairway."
      }
    ]
  },
