        "@value": "obligation"
      }
    ],
    "https://example.org/ibc/ontology/text": [
      {
        "@value": "1030.14.1 Ramped aisles. Aisles that are sloped more than 1 unit vertical in 20 units horizontal (5-percent slope) shall be considered to be a ramped aisle. Ramped aisles that serve as part of an accessible route in accordance with Sections 1009 and 1109.2 shall have a maximum slope of 1 unit vertical in 12 units horizontal (8-percent slope). The slope of other ramped aisles shall not exceed 1 unit vertical in 8 units horizontal (12.5percent slope). TABLE 1030.13.2.1 SMOKE-PROTECTED OR OPEN-AIR ASSEMBLY AISLE ACCESSWAYS For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://example.org/ibc/2021/sem-ibc2021-1025.2.5-atomic-3",
